  "title": "Treaty of Nerchinsk",
  "summary": "Russia and Qing China signed a peace treaty at Nerchinsk in Transbaikalia in 1689, ending years of conflict over the Amur region. The border ran along the Argun and Gorbitsa rivers and the Stanovoi Range, Russia gave up the Amur valley and Albazin, and regular trade between the two states was opened.",
